extends ./layout/layout-default
block content
  article.TextPage
    p.Eyebrow ABOUT THE GAME
    h1 A small game about big decisions.
    p In Hire and Seek, you run the hiring desk at Orbit Works. Scout learns from past hiring choices. You watch what happens and ask what it learned.
    p The orange applicants are from Bengaluru. The blue applicants are from Chennai. City and colour are not measures of skill.
    h2 Built on an original game
    p This classroom project adapts Survival of the Best Fit, created by Alia ElKattan, Miha Klasinc, Gabor Csapo, and Jihyun Kim.
    p We kept its animated characters, office artwork, training effects, sounds, font, and parts of its code. We added the Hire and Seek look and story, three hiring rounds, seeded applicants, real tree training, the investigation, repair workshop, calculated endings, saved progress, and an audit receipt.
    p
      a(href='https://github.com/survivalofthebestfit/survivalofthebestfit') View the original project
    h2 What is ready?
    p All six chapters are connected. Hire people, train Scout, check its questions, try a repair, and test it on 200 fresh CVs. You can save your place and download or print your receipt.
    p Automated checks cover the model and game flow. Final browser checks and beginner playtests are still pending. We do not claim learning results before people have played.
    h2 Font and artwork
    p The game uses VT323 by Peter Hull, under the SIL Open Font License. Original character art, office art, and sound come from Survival of the Best Fit. Their source and notice review are recorded in the project docs.
    a.MainButton(href='./game/') Play the current version →
